Falsifies `kernel::arch::riscv64::iommu::proofs::no_device_can_reach_another_devices_context`.

The defect is the one-level directory's stride, left in place under the two-level one:
`directory_position` picks the right leaf but offsets into it by `rid * dc_bytes` rather than by
`(rid % per_leaf) * dc_bytes`. For requester ids 0 to 63 in the extended format the two agree,
which is every device the one-frame directory held, so the edit reads as correct to anyone porting
from the old shape. For id 64 and above the context is written past the end of its leaf's single
frame into whatever the allocator handed out next.

Expected to fail: `assert!(pa.offset + dc_bytes <= page_frames::FRAME_SIZE, "every context the
bound admits lies inside its leaf's single frame")`. Confirmed red on 2026-11-11 (UTC), on an
x86_64 host, against this file's pure functions and harness compiled on their own.

The sibling harnesses stay green under this patch: `the_iommu_is_handed_exactly_the_domain_the_kernel_built`
builds a context's words and never places one, and `the_root_entry_names_exactly_the_leaf` never
places a device.

diff --git a/kernel/src/arch/riscv64/iommu.rs b/kernel/src/arch/riscv64/iommu.rs
--- a/kernel/src/arch/riscv64/iommu.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/arch/riscv64/iommu.rs
@@ -199,7 +199,7 @@
     let per_leaf = page_frames::FRAME_SIZE / dc_bytes;
     Some(DirectoryPosition {
         leaf: (rid as u64 / per_leaf) as usize,
-        offset: (rid as u64 % per_leaf) * dc_bytes,
+        offset: rid as u64 * dc_bytes,
     })
 }
 
